    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0544" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/10–2253: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-10-22T13:00:00-05:00">October 22, 1953—1
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Delga 150. Re ILC elections.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Delegation suggests Department reconsider present position (Gadel 36) which is to support Myint
                            Thein (Burma) rather than Khoman (Thailand). Reasons are: (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >a</hi>) Thailand supports US in UN far
                        more consistently than does Burma; (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) We have
                        not supported Thailand for any other post during session; (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Even though Myint Thein
                        appears better qualified, Khoman
                        appears possess necessary qualifications.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>
                        De La Colina (Mexico) informs USGADel that LA delegates do not intend caucus on ILC slate. Only agreement
                        is decision by four states now represented on ILC (Panama, Mexico, Brazil,
                        Colombia) to vote for each other. US therefore free vote for four LA nominees we consider most highly
                        qualified.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Request Department’s views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lodge</hi>
                        </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
